{"id":"word:hebrew:H4279","type":"word","title":"מָחָר","subtitle":"H4279 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"properly, deferred , i.e. the morrow ; usually (adverbially) tomorrow ; indefinitely, hereafter","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to מָחָר (H4279) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 52 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"מָחָר (mâchâr) means properly, deferred , i.e. the morrow ; usually (adverbially) tomorrow ; indefinitely, hereafter First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 19 2."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"מָחָר","transliteration":"mâchâr","pronunciation":"maw-khar'","strong":"H4279","lemmaId":"hebrew:H4279","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["מָחָר֙","מָחָ֗ר","מָחָ֖ר","מָחָ֔ר","מָחָ֑ר"],"morphs":[["HNcmsa",41],["HC/Ncmsa",6],["HR/Ncmsa",5]]},"definitions":{"short":"properly, deferred , i.e. the morrow ; usually (adverbially) tomorrow ; indefinitely, hereafter","usage":"time to come, tomorrow.","full":"H4279. machar מָחָר 52 noun masculine , used often as adverb , tomorrow, in time to come (Aramaic מְחַר ; probably properly time in front , Kö ii. 263 , compare √, and Assyrian ma—ru , front , often of time, though always of former time, of old , Dl HWB 402 ); — 1 to-morrow (the day following the present day), a. as substantive Exod 16:23 לְי קֹדֶשׁ שַׁבַּת ׳שַׁבָּתוֺן מָחָר to-morrow is a sabbath, etc., 1Sam 20:5 מָחָר חֹדֶשׁ to-morrow is the new moon, 20:18 ; in מָחָר יוֺם Gen 30:33 ; Prov 27:1 ; Isa 56:12 ; in the idiomatic phrase מָחָר כָּעֵת at the like of the time, (being) to-morrow, = about to-morrow (see כְּ 1a ) Exod 9:18 ; 1Sam 9:16 ; 20:12 ; 1Kin 19:2 ; 20:6 ; 2Kin 7:1 , 18 ; 10:6 ; and in לְמָחָר Exod 8:19 הַזֶּה הָאֹת יִהְיֶה לְמָחָר , = for, against, to-morrow , 8:6 ; Num 11:18 ; Josh 7:13 ; Est 5:12 . b. as adverb accusative Exod 8:25 ; 9:5 ׳י הַזֶּה הַדָּבָר יַעֲשֶׂה מָחָר , 10:4 אַרְבֶּה מָחָר מֵבִיא הִנְנִי , 17:9 ; 32:5 ; Num 14:25 ; 1Sam 11:9 etc., Josh 11:6 הַזּאֹת כָּעֵת מָחָר ; opposed to הַיּוֺם Exod 19:10 וּמָחָר הַיּוֺם , Josh 22:18 ; 2Sam 11:12 a; rhetorically, Isa 22:13 נָמוּת מָחָר כִּי . 2 = in future time , Exod 13:14 לֵאמֹר מָחָר בִנְךָ יִשְׁאָֽלְךָ כִּי = Deut 6:20 ; Josh 4:6 , 21 ; 22:24 , 27 , 28 ; so מָחָר בְּיוֺם Gen 30:33 .","rootNote":"probably from 309 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 19 2","keyReferences":["1Kgs 19 2","1Kgs 20 6","1Sam 9 16","1Sam 11 9","1Sam 11 10","1Sam 19 11","1Sam 20 5","1Sam 20 12"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":52,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 19 2","book":"1Kgs","chapter":19,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מָחָר֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 20 6","book":"1Kgs","chapter":20,"verse":6,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מָחָ֗ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 9 16","book":"1Sam","chapter":9,"verse":16,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מָחָ֡ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 11 9","book":"1Sam","chapter":11,"verse":9,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מָחָ֛ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 11 10","book":"1Sam","chapter":11,"verse":10,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מָחָ֖ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 19 11","book":"1Sam","chapter":19,"verse":11,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מָחָ֖ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 20 5","book":"1Sam","chapter":20,"verse":5,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מָחָ֔ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 20 12","book":"1Sam","chapter":20,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מָחָר֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 20 18","book":"1Sam","chapter":20,"verse":18,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מָחָ֣ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 28 19","book":"1Sam","chapter":